# *******************
# ECCO gradient check
# *******************
# Repaired configuration (2026-08-31): the committed data.grdchk perturbs
# xx_theta at (4,8,1), near the southern boundary where the 30-day adjoint
# sensitivity is ~6e-10 against a field maximum of ~3.9e-2 at the cost
# section, so the check divides its own noise by 2*eps and fails by ~8
# orders of magnitude -- it always has (see "Verifying correctness" in the
# root README). This variant moves the point onto the sensitivity peak
# (global i=2, j=127, k=26, the cost-section row) and raises grdchk_eps so
# the predicted response clears the perturbed-run noise floor.
# NOTE the naming trap: i/jGloPos are TILE-LOCAL (grdchk_readparms errors if
# > sNx/sNy); the tile is chosen with i/jGloTile. Global (2,127) on the
# 17x22 tiles of the 3x9 decomposition = tile (1,6), local (2,17).
 &GRDCHK_NML
 grdchk_eps       = 1.d-3,
 iGloPos          = 2,
 jGloPos          = 17,
 iGloTile         = 1,
 jGloTile         = 6,
 kGloPos          = 26,
 nstep            = 1,
 nend             = 4,
 grdchkvarname    = "xx_theta",
 &
